      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-{5}^{x}-3?$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={5}^{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14228213/assets/e85f2f0f042f85b5f7c8162b744a5c9d4688a93faf4ccddbad82ca1a9db47f93.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{5}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14228213/assets/971d4cf0310cced68f72be500d65fff26163a7e2bd5cee005e25e92ca3fb931e.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $3$ units down to give $y=-{5}^{x}-3.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,-4)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14228213/assets/8d4dd11693eda60dc0ed7eb041bdb94c90757f6bb75be3523ce77d01d28534de.png)",
